= Psionic Solitons =

== Conceptual Overview ==

In the psionics framework, a '''psionic soliton''' is a stable, localized solution of the nonlinear ψ field equation. It arises when the dispersive tendency of the wave operator (□ψ) is exactly balanced by the stabilizing nonlinear self-interaction (−λψ³).

Unlike ordinary waves that spread out and fade, solitons maintain their shape, amplitude, and coherence for extended periods. They are the mathematical embodiment of what esoteric traditions have long called “thought-forms,” “energy balls,” or “stable constructs.”

